\begin_layout Chapter
Introduction
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
grib2image is a command line application that produces images from GRIB2
 data.
 An XML based configuration file provides colormaps and specifies how grib
 values map to entries in those colormaps.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Section
Usage
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
\begin_inset listings
inline false
status open

\begin_layout Standard

grib2image config.xml [param1] [param2] [param3] ...
\end_layout

\end_inset


\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
grib2image expects a configuration file as its first parameter.
 Additional parameters depend on the contents of the configuration file.
 For simple configuration files where positional parameter placeholders
 are not used, no extra parameters are necessary.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Chapter
Configuration File
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
The configuration file is an XML document with a root element named 
\begin_inset Quotes eld
\end_inset

Grib2Image
\begin_inset Quotes erd
\end_inset

.
 Children of the root element consist of 
\begin_inset Quotes eld
\end_inset

ColorMap
\begin_inset Quotes erd
\end_inset

 element(s) and 
\begin_inset Quotes eld
\end_inset

Image
\begin_inset Quotes erd
\end_inset

 element(s).
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
At least one 
\begin_inset Quotes eld
\end_inset

ColorMap
\begin_inset Quotes erd
\end_inset

 element and one 
\begin_inset Quotes eld
\end_inset

Image
\begin_inset Quotes erd
\end_inset

 element is necessary in order for an image to be produced.
 Following is a simple configuration file that produces an image called
 
\begin_inset Quotes eld
\end_inset

out.tif
\begin_inset Quotes erd
\end_inset

 from a grib file named 
\begin_inset Quotes eld
\end_inset

in.grib
\begin_inset Quotes erd
\end_inset

.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
\begin_inset listings
inline false
status open

\begin_layout Standard

<Grib2Image>
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard

    <ColorMap label="map1" r=".5" g=".5" b=".5" a="1.0">
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard

        <Range>
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard

            <Value r=".2" g=".2" b="1.0">265</Value>
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard

            <Value>280</Value>
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard

            <Value r="1.0" b=".2">295</Value>
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard

            <Value>305</Value>
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard

        </Range>
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard

    </ColorMap>
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard

    <Image filename="out.tif" grib="in.grib" message="0" colormap="map1"/>
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard

</Grib2Image>
\end_layout

\end_inset


\end_layout

\begin_layout Section
Image element
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
The 
\emph on
Image
\emph default
 element contains 3 mandatory properties to define an image.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Itemize

\emph on
filename
\emph default
 - contains the output image filename.
 Image type is determined by the extension, and support depends on formats
 supported by libgz4d.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Itemize

\emph on
grib
\emph default
 - contains the filename of the grib file.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Itemize

\emph on
colormap
\emph default
 - contains the label of the colormap to be applied to the grib data to
 produce the image.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
Additional optional properties may also be used.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Itemize

\emph on
message
\emph default
 - Zero based index number for desired message for grib files that contain
 multiple messages.
 (Defaults to 0).
\end_layout

\begin_layout Itemize

\emph on
parameter
\emph default
 - Zero based index number for desired parameter for grib messages that
 contain multiple parameters.
 Not used is 
\emph on
message
\emph default
 property not present.
 (Defaults to 0).
\end_layout

\begin_layout Itemize

\emph on
mapOffset
\emph default
 - 
\emph on
Offset
\emph default
 parameter used for mapping.
 (Defaults to 0.0)
\end_layout

\begin_layout Itemize

\emph on
mapScale
\emph default
 - 
\emph on
Scale
\emph default
 parameter used for mapping.
 (Defaults to 1.0)
\end_layout

\begin_layout Itemize

\emph on
mapMin
\emph default
 - 
\emph on
Min
\emph default
 parameter used for mapping.
 (Defaults to minimum data value)
\end_layout

\begin_layout Itemize

\emph on
mapMax
\emph default
 - 
\emph on
Max
\emph default
 parameter used for mapping.
 (Defaults to maximum data value)
\end_layout

\begin_layout Subsection
Mapping values to a color map
\begin_inset LatexCommand label
name "sub:Mapping-values"

\end_inset


\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
Color maps are not always defined to directly map values to a color.
 Two sets of parameters may be used to map values to a color map.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Subsubsection
Offset and Scale
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
The value obtained from the grib file is first added to 
\emph on
Offset
\emph default
 and the result is multiplied by 
\emph on
Scale
\emph default
.
 The result is used to lookup the color in the color map.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
\begin_inset Formula \[
mapValue=(gribValue+Offset)Scale\]

\end_inset


\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
This method is useful when the range of the data is known and the same mapping
 is needed for multiple data sets.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Subsubsection
Min and Max
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
The values obtained from the grib file may also be transformed such that
 the data's maximum value maps to 
\emph on
Max
\emph default
 and the data's minimum value maps to 
\emph on
Min
\emph default
.
 
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
This method is useful when the extends of the data are not known and the
 results don't need to be compared with data having different extents.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Subsubsection
Specifing a mapping with both Offset/Scale and Min/Max
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
If both set of parameters are used.
 The values are first mapped to the 
\begin_inset Quotes eld
\end_inset

Min
\begin_inset Quotes erd
\end_inset

 and 
\emph on
Max
\emph default
 range before being transformed by the 
\emph on
Offset
\emph default
 and 
\emph on
Scale
\emph default
 parameters.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Subsection
Command line parameters
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
Any property of the 
\emph on
Image
\emph default
 element may contain a placeholder that gets replaced by a command line
 parameter.
 This allows for more general configuration files to be constructed.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
The format of the placeholde is the character 
\emph on
@
\emph default
 followed by the number of the command line parameter.
 Command line parameters are numbered sequentialy with 
\emph on
@1
\emph default
 refering to the first parameter followint the configuration filename.
 The following example shows an 
\emph on
Image
\emph default
 element with 2 parameter placeholders.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
\begin_inset listings
inline false
status open

\begin_layout Standard

<Image filename="@2" grib="@1" message="0" colormap="map1"/>
\end_layout

\end_inset


\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
Assuming the above element is part of a configuration file called config.xml,
 the following is a possible usage:
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
\begin_inset listings
inline false
status open

\begin_layout Standard

grib2image config.xml in.grib out.tif
\end_layout

\end_inset


\end_layout

\begin_layout Section
ColorMap element
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
A color map specifies how a color is assigned to a value.
 The 
\emph on
ColorMap
\emph default
 element contains a 
\emph on
label
\emph default
 property and may contain 
\emph on
r
\emph default
, 
\emph on
g
\emph default
, 
\emph on
b
\emph default
 or 
\emph on
a
\emph default
 properties to specify the default color.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Subsection
Range element
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
A 
\emph on
Range 
\emph default
element contains a list of 
\emph on
Value
\emph default
 elements with associated colors.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Subsubsection
Value element
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
A 
\emph on
Value
\emph default
 element defines a color for the value expressed by the element's content.
 The color component properties (
\emph on
r
\emph default
,
\emph on
g
\emph default
,
\emph on
b
\emph default
 and 
\emph on
a
\emph default
) are optional, and the unspecified components will copy the previous value's
 color component or the color map's default color if this is the first value
 specified in the range.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Subsection
Determining a color for a value
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
Given a value that has been scaled according to section 
\begin_inset LatexCommand ref
reference "sub:Mapping-values"

\end_inset

, the color is determined by starting with the color map's default color.
 
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
For every range in which the value is included, a color is determined, by
 interpolating if necessary, the colors assigned to the closest assigned
 values.
 This color is blended using its alpha value with the resulting color.
 Setting a range's alpha value to 1.0 make the range's color replace the
 resulting color.
\end_layout

